# Olmedo et al., TOPLAS 2018, Example 4.9 (p. 4:20): a fair coin chooses between diverging and
# tossing two fair coins (0 is heads) observed to show at least one head.  The probability that
# the last toss is heads is 2/7 under cwp, 6/7 under cwlp and 2/3 under r2 (wp/wp(1), which
# normalises over the terminating runs and so ignores the diverging half).
# Expected: refused with one line.  With a loop, wp(S, f) <= q * wp(S, 1) compares a least
# fixpoint with a multiple of another, which no single least fixpoint expresses, so the bound
# checker, which certifies one direction per query, cannot be asked it.  The bound 0.7 holds.
nat x;
nat y;
{
	while (true) {
		skip;
	}
}[1/2]{
	{
		x := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		x := 1;
	}
	{
		y := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		y := 1;
	}
	observe(x = 0 || y = 0);
}
?Ex [[y = 0]] <= 0.7 r2
